Subject: [PATCH] correct the wiki's api, build and getting-started pages
 against the source

wiki/API.md printed ten things src/api does not say, and eight of them break the
reader's build. The goals are in baritone.api.pathing.goals, not baritone.api.utils.
IMineProcess has no String overload - it takes BlockOptionalMetaLookup,
BlockOptionalMeta... or Block... - so mine("diamond_ore") and mine(64, "...") do not
compile. IFollowProcess declares exactly one method, follow(Predicate<Entity>), so
follow("playerName") does not either. IGameEventListener has sixteen abstract
methods and the fork ships no adapter, so the anonymous listener overriding three
cannot compile; and the interaction callback is onBlockInteract(BlockInteractEvent),
not onPlayerInteract(PlayerInteractEvent). IPathingBehavior has no getPathfinder(),
getPath() returns Optional<IPath>, the interface is ICustomGoalProcess rather than
IGoalProcess, and baritone-api-*.jar is not built here.

wiki/Building.md and wiki/Getting-Started.md both list baritone-api-*.jar,
baritone-standalone-*.jar and baritone-unoptimized-*.jar. "standalone" and
"unoptimized" appear in no build.gradle in the tree. What is declared is one jar per
loader - fabric, forge, neoforge, tweaker - in three variants: remapJar with no
classifier, built from the shadow jar's output, shadowJar as dev-shadow, and jar as
dev. The Getting-Started copy is the worse of the two, because that is the page
telling a first-time reader which file to drop in mods/.

The mine example keeps its intent by way of BlockOptionalMeta's String selector
constructor rather than becoming a block import. Building.md names the tasks and
classifiers each loader declares and points at scripts/headless/README.md as a
known-good invocation. Each page gains the source-of-truth note.

No test pins these three. A defaults table is a structured claim against one file and
SettingsWikiTest can hold it; a page of Java examples is not, and the honest pin is
to compile them. That is feasible - AimScatterTest already imports
net.minecraft.core.BlockPos, so the Minecraft API is on the test compile classpath -
but it is a bigger change than correcting the pages and is left recorded rather than
half built.

47 classes / 381 tests / 0 failures / 0 errors / 0 skipped, unchanged. No src/ file
is touched.
